(window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY = window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY || {})["2026-08-25"] = {"meta":{"id":"2026-08-25","label":"2026 年 8 月 25 日","date":"2026-08-25","range":"","theme":"科技","themes":["科技"],"sources":["The Guardian"],"title":"Appy talk: what next for dating as swipe","titleZh":"","counts":{"article":0,"paragraph":12,"vocab":70,"question":15,"qa":0,"original":4,"layout":1},"tabs":{"articles":false,"reading":true,"tests":true,"qa":false,"originals":true}},"articles":[],"reading":[{"file":"8.25 精读.pdf","headline":{"title":"Appy talk: what next for dating as swipe","titleZh":"","source":"The Guardian","series":"考研那些事儿之科技系列"},"paragraphs":[{"index":1,"en":"Bumble was supposed to be different. When the dating app launched in 2014, it offered women a simple proposition: if you matched with a man, you had to make the first move. The rule was meant to make online dating safer and less intimidating, while giving women control over who got to speak first.","zh":"Bumble本该与众不同。这款约会应用在2014年上线时，向女性提供了一个简单的设定：如果你与一位男性配对成功，你必须先主动发起对话。这一规则旨在让在线约会更安全、减少局促感，同时让女性掌握谁先发言的主动权。"},{"index":2,"en":"This week, Bumble abandoned it. The change follows the introduction of Opening Moves, which had already softened the original rule, and comes as Bumble prepares to abandon another defining feature: the swipe. The company said it was responding to changing user behaviour and wanted to encourage more meaningful connections. But there is another way of reading the changes.","zh":"本周，Bumble放弃了这一规则。这一变化紧随“开场白”（OpeningMoves）功能上线，该功能已在一定程度上放宽了原有规则。而与此同时，Bumble还准备舍弃另一个标志性功能：滑动匹配。公司表示，此举意在适应用户行为的转变，并希望促成更有意义的连接。但对此也可以有另一种解读。"},{"index":3,"en":"Bumble was created to fix what many saw as Tinder’s chaotic and aggressive hookup culture by shifting the power dynamic entirely to women. Now it is dismantling those features. And it is not alone. Across the dating app industry, the swipe-and-match model that transformed how people met is being quietly reworked while companies race to put artificial intelligence at the centre of whatever comes next.","zh":"Bumble的创立初衷，是为了修正许多人眼中Tinder那种混乱且充满攻击性的约炮文化，将权力动态完全转向女性。而现在，它正在逐步废除这些特色功能。而且，Bumble并非孤例。在整个约会应用行业，曾经彻底改变人们相识方式的“滑动与匹配”模式，正在悄然被重构，同时各大公司竞相将人工智能置于下一阶段发展的核心位置。"},{"index":4,"en":"“Bumble is in salvage mode,” said Luke Brunning, a philosopher who studies the ethics of technology and relationships. “They’ve already reorganised, restructured and cut jobs in response to declining revenue. This risky, standout pivot suggests they’re wondering how, despite all that, to keep going.”","zh":"“Bumble正处于自救模式，”研究技术与人际关系伦理的哲学家卢克·布鲁宁表示。“为了应对营收下滑，他们已经进行了重组、结构调整和裁员。这次高风险、颇为大胆的转型表明，他们在思考——尽管做了这么多努力——如何才能继续走下去。”"},{"index":5,"en":"Bumble’s paying users fell sharply over the past year and its share price has been under sustained pressure. The company cut about 30% of its workforce this year. “It’s going to be fascinating to see whether they can weather it,” Brunning said. “But they’re not alone: a lot of the major players are also in salvage mode, trying to figure out how to position themselves in a market that is increasingly fed up with them.”","zh":"过去一年，Bumble的付费用户大幅下降，其股价也持续承压。该公司今年裁减了约30%的员工。“它们能否挺过这一关，这很耐人寻味，”布鲁宁说。“但它们并非个例：许多主要玩家也处于自救模式，试图在一个越来越厌倦它们的市场中重新定位自己。”"},{"index":6,"en":"Brunning’s research shows dating apps are now often used grudgingly, because people feel they are necessary, rather than with the excitement that accompanied their rise.","zh":"布鲁宁的研究表明，如今人们使用约会应用往往是出于无奈，因为觉得不得不使用，而非像它们兴起时那样满怀期待。"},{"index":7,"en":"The online dating industry – estimated to be worth almost £10 bn globally – is keenly aware of this. Its solution? To go full AI. Grindr – seen as a testbed for the wider industry – is currently transitioning into an “AI-first” platform. Tinder is testing Chemistry, an AI-powered system intended to reduce “swipe fatigue”. Bumble has been developing an AI matchmaking assistant called Bee.","zh":"在线约会行业——全球估值接近100亿英镑——对此心知肚明。它的解决方案是什么？全面拥抱AI。被视为整个行业试验田的Grindr，目前正转型为一个“AI优先”平台。Tinder正在测试Chemistry，一个旨在减少“滑动疲劳”的AI驱动系统。Bumble也一直在开发一个名为Bee的AI匹配助手。"},{"index":8,"en":"Other start-ups are dispensing with swiping altogether. The London-based Fate describes itself as an “agentic AI dating app”: instead of browsing profiles, users are interviewed by an AI about what they want from relationships to find similarities with potential partners.","zh":"其他初创公司则完全摒弃了滑动功能。总部位于伦敦的Fate自称是一款“智能体AI约会应用”：用户无需浏览个人资料，而是由AI对用户进行访谈，了解他们在感情中的需求，从而找出与潜在伴侣之间的相似之处。"},{"index":9,"en":"So why aren’t we talking about being on the brink of a brave new world of dating apps, where AI will successfully sift the candidates to find our one true love? Why instead, is the debate about whether the apps will even survive?","zh":"那么，为什么我们并没有在谈论一个约会应用即将迎来的“美丽新世界”——在那里AI将成功筛选候选人，帮我们找到真爱？为什么反而在争论这些应用是否还能存活下去？"},{"index":10,"en":"Adam Peacock, a researcher of technology and intimacy, thinks the issue is that the industry is misreading what people are objecting to. “There’s a kind of emerging cultural backlash against allowing AI into our intimate lives as well as additional concern that someone you’re talking to on these apps is actually filtering the whole conversation through an AI concierge,” he said.","zh":"技术与亲密关系研究员亚当·皮科克认为，问题在于行业误解了人们真正反对的是什么。“目前正出现一种文化上的反弹，抵制AI介入我们的亲密生活；同时，人们也越来越担心，在这些应用上与你聊天的人，其实是在通过一个AI管家过滤整段对话，”他说。"},{"index":11,"en":"Peacock said gen Z in particular had concerns that dating apps were not even being designed to make good connections between users but were, instead, opaquely tweaked to monetise the time users spent on the sites. That, in a cynical twist, the apps were deliberately profiting from keeping people lonely. “The dating industry has turned intimacy into an enormous source of data,” said Peacock. “Dating apps can know where people live, what they look like, who they are attracted to, what they say to potential partners and, increasingly, how they behave.”","zh":"皮科克表示，Z世代尤其担心，约会应用的设计初衷甚至不是为了促成用户之间的良好连接，而是对算法进行不透明的调整，以此将用户的使用时长变现。更讽刺的是，这些应用故意从让人们保持孤独中获利。“约会行业已经把亲密关系变成了巨大的数据来源，”皮科克说。“约会应用可以知道人们住在哪里、长什么样、被谁吸引、对潜在伴侣说了什么，而且越来越多地，它们还能知道人们的行为方式。”"},{"index":12,"en":"But the first generation of dating apps – the era of the profile, the swipe, the match and the message – may be reaching its end. Peacock thinks the apps may evolve into something broader: “more of a social media, lifestyle product than a dedicated dating app”. But the question is whether any iteration of dating app will make dating better, or whether the extra layers of AI will simply function as a temporary facade on an exhausted model.","zh":"但第一代约会应用——那个由个人资料、滑动、配对和消息组成的时代——可能正在走向终结。皮科克认为，这些应用可能会演变成更广泛的形态：“更像是一个社交媒体、生活方式类产品，而不仅仅是专门的约会应用。”但问题在于，无论约会应用如何迭代，它是否真的能让约会变得更好，还是说，新增的AI层不过是给一个已经过时的模式暂时披上光鲜的外衣。"}],"vocab":[{"term":"swipe","head":"n. /swaɪp/ to move your finger over the screen of a","definition":"mobile phone or tablet in order to move onto the next","gloss":"","example":"page, choose something, etc. 滑动（屏幕操作）","exampleZh":"Swipe left to see more search results. 左滑查看更多搜索结 果。[swipe还可以用来指刷卡时“刷”的动作]","tags":[]},{"term":"fatigue","head":"n. /fəˈtiːɡ/ a feeling of extreme tiredness, usually","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"resulting from hard work or exercise 疲劳，劳累【️【️考研大纲","exampleZh":"词汇】 Depression is also a major cause of fatigue. 抑郁症也是导致 疲劳的一个主要原因。","tags":[]},{"term":"launch","head":"v. /lɔːntʃ/ to begin something such as a plan, or","definition":"","gloss":"introduce something new such as a product 推出，发起，启","example":"The company plans to launch a new feature next month.","exampleZh":"动【️【️考研大纲词汇】 该公司计划下个月推出一项新功能。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"proposition","head":"n. /ˌprɒpəˈzɪʃən/ an offer or suggestion,","definition":"","gloss":"usuallyinbusiness（通常指商业上的）提议，建议【️【️考研大","example":"He wrote to me with a very interesting business","exampleZh":"纲词汇】 proposition.他给我写信，提出了一个非常有趣的商业提议。","tags":[]},{"term":"intimidating","head":"adj. /ɪnˈtɪmɪdeɪtɪŋ/ making you feel","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"frightenedornervous令人紧张的，吓人的","exampleZh":"She can be very intimidating when she's angry. 她发怒的时 候会非常吓人。","tags":[]},{"term":"control","head":"n. /kənˈtrəʊl/ the ability to make someone or","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"somethingdowhatyouwant控制（权）；支配（权）【️【️考研","exampleZh":"大纲词汇】 She wants to have more control over her daily schedule. 她 希望对日常安排有更多控制。[undercontrol得到控制] Bumble本该与众不同。这款约会应用在2014年上线时， 向女性提供了一个简单的设定：如果你与一位男性配对成功， 你必须先主动发起对话。这一规则旨在让在线约会更安全、减 少局促感，同时让女性掌握谁先发言的主动权。","tags":[]},{"term":"abandon","head":"v. /əˈbændən/ to leave a place, thing, or person","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"permanently放弃，抛弃【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"He abandoned his car in the snow. 他把汽车丢弃在雪地里。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"soften","head":"v. /ˈsɒfən/ to make something less severe, strong,","definition":"","gloss":"orunpleasant（使）减轻，（使）缓和","example":"The new policy aims to soften the impact of the changes.","exampleZh":"新政策旨在减轻这些变化带来的影响。[反义：harden（使）变 严厉，（使）变坚强，（使）变冷酷]","tags":[]},{"term":"defining","head":"adj. /dɪˈfaɪnɪŋ/ very important because it shows","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"the essential character of something 决定性的，标志性的","exampleZh":"His defining quality is his honesty. 他的标志性品质是诚实。","tags":[]},{"term":"encourage","head":"v. /ɪnˈkʌrɪdʒ/ to make someone more likely to","definition":"do something, or to make something more likely to happen","gloss":"","example":"鼓励，促进【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"Good weather encourages people to go outside. 好天气会 促使人们到户外去。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"read","head":"v. /ˈriːd/ to understand and give a particular meaning","definition":"","gloss":"to written information, a statement, a situation, etc. 理解；","example":"If I’ve read the situation correctly, we should have some","exampleZh":"读作；（用于订正讹误）改作，换用 agreement on the contract by the end of the week. 如果我 对形势的看法正确的话，周末前我们应该可以就合同达成某种一 致。 本周，Bumble放弃了这一规则。这一变化紧随“开场白” （OpeningMoves）功能上线，该功能已在一定程度上放宽了 原有规则。而与此同时，Bumble还准备舍弃另一个标志性功 能：滑动匹配。公司表示，此举意在适应用户行为的转变，并 希望促成更有意义的连接。但对此也可以有另一种解读。","tags":[]},{"term":"chaotic","head":"adj. /keɪˈɒtɪk/ in a state of complete confusion","definition":"","gloss":"anddisorder混乱的，无秩序的","example":"The traffic in the city is completely chaotic during rush","exampleZh":"hour.这座城市在高峰时段的交通完全是一片混乱。[orderly adj.整齐的；井然有序的]","tags":[]},{"term":"hookup","head":"n. /ˈhʊkʌp/ a sexual relationship or encounter,","definition":"","gloss":"often casual and without commitment （尤指非正式的）性","example":"Many dating apps are known for facilitating casual","exampleZh":"关系，约炮 hookups rather than long-term relationships. 许多约会应用 以促进随意的约炮而非长期关系而闻名。","tags":[]},{"term":"dynamic","head":"n. /daɪˈnæmɪk/ the way in which people or","definition":"","gloss":"things behave and interact with each other 动态，互动关系","example":"The dynamic between the two teammates changed after","exampleZh":"【️【️考研大纲词汇】 they had a serious conversation. 两位队友在认真交谈之后， 他们之间的互动关系发生了变化。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"dismantle","head":"v. /dɪsˈmæntəl/ to take apart or destroy","definition":"","gloss":"something, especially a system or set of rules 拆除，废除","example":"The government plans to dismantle the old healthcare","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"transform","head":"v. /trænsˈfɔːm/ to change completely the","definition":"","gloss":"appearance, character, or function of something 彻底改","example":"The new manager transformed the company's working","exampleZh":"变，改造【️【️考研大纲词汇】 culturewithinmonths.新经理在几个月内彻底改变了公司的工 作文化。[transformer adj. 变压器]","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"intelligence","head":"n. /ɪnˈtelɪdʒəns/ the ability to learn,","definition":"","gloss":"understand, and think in a logical way about things 智力，","example":"These magnificent ancient buildings demonstrate the great","exampleZh":"智慧【️【️考研大纲词汇】 intelligence of the labouring people. 这些壮丽的古代建筑显 示了劳动人民的高度智慧.[intelligentadj.有才智的；聪颖的， 理解力强的] Bumble的创立初衷，是为了修正许多人眼中Tinder那种 混乱且充满攻击性的约炮文化，将权力动态完全转向女性。而 现在，它正在逐步废除这些特色功能。而且，Bumble并非孤 例。在整个约会应用行业，曾经彻底改变人们相识方式的“滑 动与匹配”模式，正在悄然被重构，同时各大公司竞相将人工 智能置于下一阶段发展的核心位置。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"salvage","head":"n. /ˈsælvɪdʒ/ the act of saving something from a","definition":"","gloss":"dangerousordifficultsituation（在危险或困境中的）挽救，","example":"The company's latest project was a salvage attempt to","exampleZh":"抢救 regaincustomertrust.该公司的最新项目是一次挽救行动，旨 在重新赢得客户信任。","tags":[]},{"term":"philosopher","head":"n. /fɪˈlɒsəfər/ a person who studies or writes","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"about philosophy 哲学家","exampleZh":"She is a philosopher who specializes in ethics. 她是一位专 攻伦理学的哲学家。","tags":[]},{"term":"restructure","head":"v. /ˌriːˈstrʌktʃər/ to organize a company,","definition":"business, or system in a new way to make it work more","gloss":"effectively重组，调整结构","example":"The company decided to restructure its management","exampleZh":"team.公司决定重组其管理团队。","tags":[]},{"term":"standout","head":"adj. /ˈstændaʊt/ noticeably better or more","definition":"","gloss":"impressivethanothers突出的，引人注目的","example":"Her performance was the standout moment of the","exampleZh":"concert.她的表演是音乐会最出彩的时刻。","tags":[]},{"term":"pivot","head":"n. /ˈpɪvət/ a movement in which a player turns","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"quickly while keeping one foot on the ground 转身；旋转","exampleZh":"(运动) The basketball player’s pivot was flawless. 这位篮球运动员 的转身动作完美无缺。 “Bumble正处于自救模式，”研究技术与人际关系伦理的 哲学家卢克·布鲁宁表示。“为了应对营收下滑，他们已经进行 了重组、结构调整和裁员。这次高风险、颇为大胆的转型表明， 他们在思考——尽管做了这么多努力——如何才能继续走下 去。”","tags":[]},{"term":"sharply","head":"adv. /ˈʃɑːpli/ suddenly and by a large amount 急剧","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"地，大幅地","exampleZh":"Prices dropped sharply after the announcement. 公告发布 后，价格急剧下跌。","tags":[]},{"term":"sustained","head":"adj. /səˈsteɪnd/ continuing for a long time 持续","definition":"","gloss":"的，持久的","example":"The team made a sustained effort to complete the project","exampleZh":"ontime.团队为按时完成项目做出了持续的努力。","tags":[]},{"term":"workforce","head":"n. /ˈwɜːkfɔːs/ the group of people who work in","definition":"","gloss":"a company, industry, or country 劳动力，全体员工","example":"The company has reduced its workforce by 20% this year.","exampleZh":"该公司今年已将员工人数削减了20%。[workloadn.工作量， 工作负荷]","tags":[]},{"term":"fascinating","head":"adj. /ˈfæsəneɪtɪŋ/ extremely interesting 极有趣","definition":"","gloss":"的，迷人的","example":"The book offers a fascinating glimpse of the lives of the rich","exampleZh":"andfamous.这本书使我们得以一窥富豪名流的生活，十分有趣。 过去一年，Bumble的付费用户大幅下降，其股价也持续 承压。该公司今年裁减了约30%的员工。“它们能否挺过这一 关，这很耐人寻味，”布鲁宁说。“但它们并非个例：许多主要 玩家也处于自救模式，试图在一个越来越厌倦它们的市场中重 新定位自己。”","tags":[]},{"term":"grudgingly","head":"adv. /ˈɡrʌdʒɪŋli/ in a way that shows you are","definition":"","gloss":"unwilling to do something 勉强地，不情愿地","example":"He grudgingly accepted that he would retire after the","exampleZh":"generalelection.他勉强接受了他将在大选后退休的事实。 布鲁宁的研究表明，如今人们使用约会应用往往是出于无 奈，因为觉得不得不使用，而非像它们兴起时那样满怀期待。","tags":[]},{"term":"keenly","head":"adv. /ˈkiːnli/ in a way that shows you are very","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"aware or interested in something 强烈地，敏锐地","exampleZh":"She is keenly aware of the risks involved. 她敏锐地意识到所 涉及的风险。","tags":[]},{"term":"testbed","head":"n. /ˈtestbed/ a place or situation used for testing","definition":"","gloss":"new ideas, products, or systems 试验台，测试平台","example":"The city is used as a testbed for new traffic management","exampleZh":"systems.该城市被用作新交通管理系统的测试平台。","tags":[]},{"term":"transition","head":"v. /trænˈzɪʃən/ to change from one state or","definition":"","gloss":"conditiontoanother转变，过渡【️【️考研大纲词汇】","example":"Many companies are transitioning to remote work models.","exampleZh":"许多公司正在向远程工作模式过渡。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"intend","head":"v. /ɪnˈtend/ to have a plan or purpose in mind 打算，","definition":"","gloss":"计划【️【️考研大纲词汇】","example":"Somehow, I offended him, which wasn't what I'd intended.","exampleZh":"我不知怎么得罪了他，但这不是我的初衷。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"reduce","head":"v. /rɪˈdjuːs/ to make something smaller in size,","definition":"","gloss":"amount,degree,etc.减少，降低【️【️考研大纲词汇】","example":"We bought a TV that was reduced from £500 to £350 in the","exampleZh":"sales.我们在大减价时，买了一台从500英镑减至350英镑的电 视。[increasev.增加，提高] 在线约会行业——全球估值接近100亿英镑——对此心知 肚明。它的解决方案是什么？全面拥抱AI。被视为整个行业试 验田的Grindr，目前正转型为一个“AI优先”平台。Tinder正 在测试Chemistry，一个旨在减少“滑动疲劳”的AI驱动系统。 Bumble也一直在开发一个名为Bee的AI匹配助手。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"start-up","head":"n. /ˈstɑːt ʌp/ a new business or company that is","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"just beginning 初创公司","exampleZh":"Many tech start-ups fail within their first two years. 许多科 技初创公司在头两年内就倒闭了。","tags":[]},{"term":"dispense with something/someone phrasalverb","head":"","definition":"/dɪˈspens/ to get rid of or stop using something or","gloss":"someonethatyoudonotneed免除；废止；省去；不再使","example":"They've had to dispense with a lot of luxuries since Mike","exampleZh":"用 losthisjob.由于迈克丢了工作，他们不得不与奢侈生活告别。","tags":[]},{"term":"browse","head":"v. /braʊz/ to look through a book, magazine,","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"website, etc. without reading everything 浏览【️【️考研大纲词","exampleZh":"汇】 I like to browse online shops in my free time. 我喜欢在空闲 时浏览网店。","tags":[]},{"term":"profile","head":"n. /ˈprəʊfaɪl/ a short description of someone's life,","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"character,work,etc.简介，个人资料【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"He updated his dating profile with new photos. 他用新照片 更新了自己的约会资料。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"similarity","head":"n. /ˌsɪmɪˈlærəti/ the state of being similar or like","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"something else 相似性","exampleZh":"There is a striking similarity between the two paintings. 这 两幅画之间有着惊人的相似之处。","tags":[]},{"term":"potential","head":"adj. /pəˈtenʃəl/ possible or likely, but not yet","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"achievedordeveloped潜在的，可能的【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"The company is looking for potential investors. 公司正在寻 找潜在的投资者。 其他初创公司则完全摒弃了滑动功能。总部位于伦敦的 Fate自称是一款“智能体AI约会应用”：用户无需浏览个人资 料，而是由AI对用户进行访谈，了解他们在感情中的需求，从 而找出与潜在伴侣之间的相似之处。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"brink","head":"n. /brɪŋk/ the point or edge where a new or","definition":"","gloss":"different situation is about to begin 边缘，临界点","example":"The country is on the brink of a major economic reform.","exampleZh":"该国正处于重大经济改革的边缘。","tags":[]},{"term":"brave","head":"adj. /breɪv/ showing no fear of dangerous or","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"difficultthings勇敢的，无畏的","exampleZh":"It was a brave decision to start his own business. 创业是一 个勇敢的决定。","tags":[]},{"term":"sift","head":"v. /sɪft/ to separate or sort through something","definition":"","gloss":"carefully in order to find what is useful or important 筛选，","example":"The police sifted through all the evidence to find the truth.","exampleZh":"仔细检查 警方仔细筛选所有证据以查明真相。[形近：shiftv.（尤指略微 地）移动；改变；转移]","tags":[]},{"term":"candidate","head":"n. /ˈkændɪdət/ a person who is being considered","definition":"","gloss":"for a job, position, or, in this context, a potential partner 候","example":"There were many excellent candidates for the scholarship.","exampleZh":"选人，人选【️【️考研大纲词汇】 该奖学金有很多优秀的候选人。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"debate","head":"n. /dɪˈbeɪt/ a discussion or argument about a","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"subject, often with different opinions 讨论，辩论【️【️考研大纲","exampleZh":"词汇】 The debate over climate change continues to intensify. 关 于气候变化的争论仍在加剧。 那么，为什么我们并没有在谈论一个约会应用即将迎来的 “美丽新世界”——在那里AI将成功筛选候选人，帮我们找到 真爱？为什么反而在争论这些应用是否还能存活下去？","tags":[]},{"term":"intimacy","head":"n. /ˈɪntɪməsi/ a close personal relationship with","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"someone, involving emotional or physical closeness 亲密，","exampleZh":"亲近 Building intimacy takes time and trust. 建立亲密关系需要时 间和信任。","tags":[]},{"term":"misread","head":"v. /ˌmɪsˈriːd/ to understand something incorrectly","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"误解，误读","exampleZh":"I misread her silence as agreement. 我误以为她的沉默是同 意。","tags":[]},{"term":"object","head":"v. /əbˈdʒekt/ to feel or express opposition or","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"disagreement反对，不赞成【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"Would anyone object if we started the meeting now? 如果 我们现在开始开会，有人反对吗？","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"emerging","head":"adj. /ɪˈmɜːdʒɪŋ/ starting to exist or become","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"known新兴的，出现的","exampleZh":"Emerging technologies are changing our daily lives. 新兴技 术正在改变我们的日常生活。","tags":[]},{"term":"backlash","head":"n. /ˈbæklæʃ/ a strong negative reaction to","definition":"","gloss":"something, especially to a social or political change （尤指","example":"There has been a backlash against the use of AI in hiring.","exampleZh":"对社会或政治变革的）强烈反对，反弹 在招聘中使用人工智能引发了强烈反对。","tags":[]},{"term":"intimate","head":"adj. /ˈɪntɪmət/ private and personal, often relating","definition":"","gloss":"tocloserelationships亲密的，私人的【️【️考研大纲词汇】","example":"They shared an intimate conversation late into the night.","exampleZh":"他们深夜进行了一次私密的交谈。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"additional","head":"adj. /əˈdɪʃənəl/ extra; more than what was","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"alreadymentioned额外的，附加的【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"We need additional time to complete the project. 我们需要 额外的时间来完成这个项目。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"actually","head":"adv. /ˈæktʃuəli/ used to say that something is","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"true, especially when the truth is surprising 实际上，事实上","exampleZh":"I didn't actually see her - I just heard her voice. 实际上我并 没有看见她，只是听到了她的声音。","tags":[]},{"term":"filter","head":"v. /ˈfɪltər/ to remove unwanted things or information","definition":"from something, or to pass something through a device","gloss":"","example":"thatdoesthis过滤，筛选【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"The system filters out spam emails automatically. 该系统会 自动过滤垃圾邮件。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"concierge","head":"n. /ˌkɒnsiˈeəʒ/ someone employed by a large","definition":"company to do jobs, such as shopping, for other","gloss":"employeeswhoareworking大公司雇用的为其他员工服务","example":"Staff perks include a concierge, an ironing service,","exampleZh":"（如采购）的雇员 discounted concert tickets, and an on-site creche. 员工福利 包括礼宾服务、熨烫服务、折扣音乐会门票和现场托儿所。 技术与亲密关系研究员亚当·皮科克认为，问题在于行业误 解了人们真正反对的是什么。“目前正出现一种文化上的反弹， 抵制AI介入我们的亲密生活；同时，人们也越来越担心，在这 些应用上与你聊天的人，其实是在通过一个AI管家过滤整段对 话，”他说。","tags":[]},{"term":"particular","head":"adj. /pəˈtɪkjələr/ relating to one person or thing","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"andnotothers特定的，特别的【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"She wanted a particular type of cactus. 她要某一特定品种的 仙人掌。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"opaquely","head":"adv. /əʊˈpeɪkli/ in a way that is not clear or easy","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"tounderstand不透明地，含糊地","exampleZh":"The contract was opaquely worded. 这份合同措辞含糊不 清。","tags":[]},{"term":"tweak","head":"v. /twiːk/ to change something slightly, especially in","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"order to make it more effective 微调，稍作调整","exampleZh":"We need to tweak the design a bit. 我们需要稍微调整一下设 计。","tags":[]},{"term":"monetise","head":"v. /ˈmʌnɪtaɪz/ to make money from something","definition":"","gloss":"将……变现，从……获利","example":"The company monetises its content through","exampleZh":"advertisements.该公司通过广告将其内容变现。","tags":[]},{"term":"cynical","head":"adj. /ˈsɪnɪkəl/ believing that people are only","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"interested in themselves and are not sincere 认为人皆自私","exampleZh":"的，愤世嫉俗的 I've always been deeply cynical about politicians. 我对政客 们总是嗤之以鼻。","tags":[]},{"term":"twist","head":"n. /twɪst/ an unexpected change in a situation 转折，","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"意外变化","exampleZh":"The plot has an interesting twist. 情节有一个有趣的转折。","tags":[]},{"term":"deliberately","head":"adv. /dɪˈlɪbərətli/ intentionally, not by","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"accident故意地，蓄意地","exampleZh":"I'm sure he says these things deliberately to annoy me. 我 敢肯定他是故意说这些来气我的。","tags":[]},{"term":"profit","head":"v. /ˈprɒfɪt/ to get money or an advantage from","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"something获利，得益【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"The company profits from selling user data. 该公司通过出售 用户数据获利。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"enormous","head":"adj. /ɪˈnɔːməs/ extremely large 巨大的【️【️考研大","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"纲词汇】","exampleZh":"He earns an enormous salary. 他工资极高。 皮科克表示，Z世代尤其担心，约会应用的设计初衷甚至 不是为了促成用户之间的良好连接，而是对算法进行不透明的 调整，以此将用户的使用时长变现。更讽刺的是，这些应用故 意从让人们保持孤独中获利。“约会行业已经把亲密关系变成了 巨大的数据来源，”皮科克说。“约会应用可以知道人们住在哪 里、长什么样、被谁吸引、对潜在伴侣说了什么，而且越来越 多地，它们还能知道人们的行为方式。”","tags":[]},{"term":"era","head":"n. /ˈɪərə/ a period of time in history that is special for","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"a particular reason 时代，纪元","exampleZh":"The digital era has changed everything. 数字时代改变了一 切。","tags":[]},{"term":"evolve","head":"v. /ɪˈvɒlv/ to develop gradually 进化，演变，发展","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"The company evolved from a small start-up. 这家公司从一家 小型初创企业演变而来。[evolutionn.演化，进化；发展，演 变]","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"lifestyle","head":"n. /ˈlaɪfstaɪl/ the way that someone lives 生活方式","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"She needs a pretty high income to support her lifestyle. 她","exampleZh":"需要相当高的收入来维持她的生活方式。","tags":[]},{"term":"iteration","head":"n. /ˌɪtərˈeɪʃən/ a new version of something, or a","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"repetition of a process 迭代，新版本","exampleZh":"The latest iteration of the software is faster. 该软件的最新迭 代运行更快。","tags":[]},{"term":"layer","head":"n. /ˈleɪər/ a level or part of something, especially a","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"thinone层，层次【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"There is a layer of dust on the shelf. 架子上有一层灰尘。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"function","head":"v. /ˈfʌŋkʃən/ to work or operate 运行，起作用【️【️考","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"The function of the veins is to carry blood to the heart. 静 脉的功能是将血液输送回心脏。","tags":[]},{"term":"façade n. /fəˈsɑːd/ a false appearance that hides the truth","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"假象，外表","exampleZh":"Behind his friendly façade, he was lonely. 在他友善的外表 下，他很孤独。","tags":[]},{"term":"exhausted","head":"adj. /ɪɡˈzɔːstɪd/ completely used up or worn","definition":"","gloss":"out耗尽的，精疲力尽的","example":"15 August 2026 | The Guardian","exampleZh":"The old system is exhausted and needs replacement. 旧的 系统已经耗尽了，需要更换。 但第一代约会应用——那个由个人资料、滑动、配对和消 息组成的时代——可能正在走向终结。皮科克认为，这些应用 可能会演变成更广泛的形态：“更像是一个社交媒体、生活方式 类产品，而不仅仅是专门的约会应用。”但问题在于，无论约会 应用如何迭代，它是否真的能让约会变得更好，还是说，新增 的AI层不过是给一个已经过时的模式暂时披上光鲜的外衣。 群公告学习流程精读，","tags":[]}]}],"tests":[{"file":"【福利】8.25 检验题__阅读理解.docx","type":"reading","instructions":[],"passage":[],"items":[{"number":21,"stem":"According to Paragraphs 1-3, what did Bumble abandon this week?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the Opening Moves feature that softened its original rule"},{"key":"B","text":"the swipe that had defined the app's matchmaking process"},{"key":"C","text":"the rule that women had to send the first message after matching"},{"key":"D","text":"the AI assistant designed to help users start conversations"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·事实识别","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 1-3","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：When the dating app launched in 2014, it offered women a simple proposition: if you matched with a man, you had to make the first move.","- 原文（Para.2）：This week, Bumble abandoned it.","- 原文（Para.3）：The change follows the introduction of Opening Moves, which had already softened the original rule, and comes as Bumble prepares to abandon another defining feature: the swipe.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：细节杂糅陷阱。Opening Moves 已经弱化原规则，但本周放弃的 it 指女性先发消息这一原规则。","- 选项B（错误）：时态与状态陷阱。原文说 prepares to abandon the swipe，是准备放弃，不是本周已经放弃。","- 选项C（正确）：Para.1 定义 Bumble 的规则：女性匹配男性后必须先行动；Para.2 的 it 正指这一规则，本周被放弃。","- 选项D（错误）：无中生有陷阱。Bee 是后文提到的 AI matchmaking assistant，不是本周放弃的规则。","【命题技巧】","- 指代关系：题眼是 abandoned it 中 it 的指代对象，需要回到 Para.1 的 proposition。","- 时间限定：B 项利用 prepares to abandon 与 abandoned 的时态差制造干扰。"]},{"number":22,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraphs 4-10 that \"another way of reading the changes\" is that Bumble's pivot is partly _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a response to commercial pressure and fading user enthusiasm rather than purely a user-centred reform"},{"key":"B","text":"proof that women-first design made online dating completely safe"},{"key":"C","text":"an isolated experiment unrelated to the wider dating-app market"},{"key":"D","text":"a strategy that has already restored revenue and stabilised its share price"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"[A]","analysis":["【题型】推理判断题·商业动机推理","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 4-10","【解析】","- 原文（Para.4）：The company said it was responding to changing user behaviour and wanted to encourage more meaningful connections. But there is another way of reading the changes.","- 原文（Para.7）：“They’ve already reorganised, restructured and cut jobs in response to declining revenue. This risky, standout pivot suggests they’re wondering how, despite all that, to keep going.”","- 原文（Para.10）：Brunning’s research shows dating apps are now often used grudgingly, because people feel they are necessary, rather than with the excitement that accompanied their rise.","分析：","- 选项A（正确）：公司宣称回应行为变化、促进有意义连接，但后文提到收入下滑、裁员、股价承压和用户厌倦。另一种解读是转型带有求生和商业压力，而不只是用户中心改革。","- 选项B（错误）：过度推理陷阱。原文说规则旨在使约会更安全，并未证明它完全实现了安全。","- 选项C（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。Para.6 和 Para.9 都强调 Bumble 不是孤例，整个行业也在重组模式。","- 选项D（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。原文说付费用户下降、股价持续承压，并未说收入已恢复、股价已稳定。","【命题技巧】","- 官方叙事与隐含动机对比：正确项需要把公司说法与 declining revenue、grudgingly 等证据并置。","- 程度控制：选项 A 使用 partly 和 rather than purely，避免把商业动机绝对化。"]},{"number":23,"stem":"Which of the following correctly describes the AI projects mentioned in Paragraphs 11 and 12?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Tinder's Chemistry is intended to intensify the fatigue caused by repeated swiping"},{"key":"B","text":"Bumble has already replaced human matchmaking with an assistant called Bee"},{"key":"C","text":"Fate asks users to browse AI-generated profiles before chatting with partners"},{"key":"D","text":"Grindr is becoming an AI-first platform, while Fate uses AI interviews to find similarities between users"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"[D]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·信息归属辨析","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 11-12","【解析】","- 原文（Para.11）：Grindr – seen as a testbed for the wider industry – is currently transitioning into an “AI-first” platform. Tinder is testing Chemistry, an AI-powered system intended to reduce “swipe fatigue”. Bumble has been developing an AI matchmaking assistant called Bee.","- 原文（Para.12）：Instead of browsing profiles, users are interviewed by an AI about what they want from relationships to find similarities with potential partners.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。Tinder 的 Chemistry 目标是 reduce swipe fatigue，不是加剧疲劳。","- 选项B（错误）：过度推理陷阱。Bumble 一直在开发 Bee，但原文没有说已完全取代人类撮合。","- 选项C（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。Fate 的特点是 instead of browsing profiles，即不再浏览档案，而是由 AI 访问用户。","- 选项D（正确）：Para.11 明确说 Grindr 正转向 AI-first，Para.12 说明 Fate 通过 AI 访谈了解用户需求并寻找与潜在伴侣的相似点。D 项信息归属正确。","【命题技巧】","- 多点核对：本题涉及 Grindr、Tinder、Bumble、Fate 四个项目，需逐项回文识别归属。","- 开发状态辨析：B 项将 developing 偷换为 already replaced，考查时态和实施程度。"]},{"number":24,"stem":"According to Paragraphs 14-17, Peacock believes that the industry's AI-centred solutions fail to address _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the technical difficulty of matching people through shared interests"},{"key":"B","text":"users' distrust of AI in intimate life and suspicion that apps profit from prolonging loneliness"},{"key":"C","text":"young users' demand for more opaque algorithms and subscription fees"},{"key":"D","text":"the shortage of personal data available to dating platforms"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】人物观点题·观点归属辨析","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 14-17","【解析】","- 原文（Para.14）：Adam Peacock...thinks the issue is that the industry is misreading what people are objecting to.","- 原文（Para.15）：“There’s a kind of emerging cultural backlash against allowing AI into our intimate lives as well as additional concern that someone you’re talking to on these apps is actually filtering the whole conversation through an AI concierge,” he said.","- 原文（Para.16）：...the apps were deliberately profiting from keeping people lonely.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：答非所问陷阱。Peacock 讨论的是用户对 AI 进入亲密生活和平台动机的不信任，不是共同兴趣匹配的技术难度。","- 选项B（正确）：Peacock 认为行业误读了用户反对的对象：用户反感 AI 深入亲密生活、担心对话被 AI 过滤，也怀疑平台不透明地调整以获利，甚至靠延续孤独赚钱。B 项完整概括。","- 选项C（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。原文批评 opaquely tweaked；用户需要的应是透明，而不是更不透明。","- 选项D（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。Para.17 说行业已把亲密关系变成巨大数据源，平台能知道大量个人信息，不是数据不足。","【命题技巧】","- 人物观点与行业方案对照：题干问 fail to address，答案须落在 Peacock 指出的信任、隐私和商业动机问题。","- 原文关键词反转：C、D 分别把 opaque 和 data abundance 反转为用户要求和数据短缺。"]},{"number":25,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Women First No More: Why Bumble Lost Its Brand Identity"},{"key":"B","text":"Brave New Love: AI Has Already Solved Swipe Fatigue"},{"key":"C","text":"Data Romance: How Dating Apps Protect Users from Algorithms"},{"key":"D","text":"Swipe Fatigue: Dating Apps Search for Survival Behind an AI Facade"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"[D]","analysis":["【题型】主旨大意题·最佳标题","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Full text","【解析】","- 原文（Para.6）：...the swipe-and-match model...is being quietly reworked while companies race to put artificial intelligence at the centre of whatever comes next.","- 原文（Para.11）：The online dating industry... Its solution? To go full AI.","- 原文（Para.21）：...whether the extra layers of AI will simply function as a temporary facade on an exhausted model.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：以偏概全陷阱。Bumble 放弃女性先发消息是引入行业变化的案例，但全文还讨论 Grindr、Tinder、Fate、用户信任和 AI 方案。","- 选项B（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。原文质疑 AI 是否能拯救约会应用，没有说它已经解决滑动疲劳。","- 选项C（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。文章强调平台掌握大量数据并可能不透明地变现，不是平台已保护用户免受算法影响。","- 选项D（正确）：标题同时抓住 swipe fatigue、行业求生和 AI 可能只是 exhausted model 上的 temporary facade 三个核心要素，符合全文从 Bumble 转型扩展到行业危机与争议的结构。","【命题技巧】","- 核心隐喻利用：temporary facade 来自尾段，是概括作者质疑 AI 方案的关键表达。","- 个案与行业关系：正确标题不限于 Bumble，而要覆盖整个约会应用行业的转型与困境。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语阅读理解大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。","如果对答案解析有疑惑，直接打开任何AI大模型（如Deepseek、Kimi等），上传该篇原文文档，然后复制粘贴对应的题目和选项，说清楚你的疑问，大模型会回应解释对应的问题。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】8.25检验题__完型填空.docx","type":"cloze","instructions":["Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)"],"passage":["Bumble was supposed to be different. When the dating app launched in 2014, it ____【11】____ women a simple ____【12】____: if you matched with a man, you had to make the ____【13】____ move. The rule was meant to make online dating safer and less ____【14】____, while giving women control over who got to speak first.","The change follows the introduction of Opening Moves, which had already ____【15】____ the original rule, and comes as Bumble prepares to abandon another defining feature: the swipe.","The company said it was ____【16】____ to changing user behaviour and wanted to encourage more meaningful ____【17】____. But there is another way of ____【18】____ the changes.","Bumble was created to fix what many saw as Tinder’s chaotic and aggressive hookup culture by shifting the power dynamic entirely to women.","Now it is ____【19】____ those features. And it is not alone. Across the dating app industry, the swipe-and-match model that transformed how people met is being quietly ____【20】____ while companies race to put artificial intelligence at the centre of whatever comes next."],"items":[{"number":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"denied"},{"key":"B","text":"offered"},{"key":"C","text":"demanded"},{"key":"D","text":"promised"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (offered)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·动宾搭配","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] denied（否认/拒绝给予）：方向相反，Bumble 不是拒绝女性这一选项。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] offered（提供）：offered women a simple proposition 指给女性提供一个简单方案。正确答案。","[C] demanded（要求）：demanded women a proposition 搭配不当。搭配干扰。","[D] promised（承诺）：语义接近，但 proposition 是产品规则而非未来承诺。近义干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"instruction"},{"key":"B","text":"permission"},{"key":"C","text":"proposition"},{"key":"D","text":"preference"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (proposition)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·语义精确度","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] instruction（指令）：语气过强，用户可选择的商业方案不是强制指令。程度差异干扰。","[B] permission（许可）：与后文“你必须先开口”的规则内容不符。语义场干扰。","[C] proposition（主张、方案）：a simple proposition 指产品给用户的简单使用方案。正确答案。","[D] preference（偏好）：可通但不精准，后文是规则设计。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"bold"},{"key":"B","text":"polite"},{"key":"C","text":"final"},{"key":"D","text":"first"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (first)","analysis":["【题型】固定搭配·形容词位置","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] bold（大胆的）：make a bold move 可通，但后文明确说女性先发消息。近义干扰。","[B] polite（礼貌的）：语义可通但不是固定搭配核心。语义场干扰。","[C] final（最后的）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] first（第一的）：make the first move 是固定搭配，意为“迈出第一步/先行动”。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"intimidating"},{"key":"B","text":"rewarding"},{"key":"C","text":"efficient"},{"key":"D","text":"expensive"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (intimidating)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·情感色彩","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第3句","【解析】","[A] intimidating（令人生畏的）：safer and less intimidating 表示“更安全、更不让人胆怯”。正确答案。","[B] rewarding（有回报的）：方向相反，规则目的不是减少回报。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] efficient（高效的）：与用户心理压力无关。语义场干扰。","[D] expensive（昂贵的）：应用本身的花费不是此处焦点。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"tightened"},{"key":"B","text":"softened"},{"key":"C","text":"preserved"},{"key":"D","text":"defended"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (softened)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·语义方向","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第1句","【解析】","[A] tightened（收紧）：与 eventually abandoned 的整体放宽趋势相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] softened（软化、放宽）：Opening Moves 先放宽了原始规则，为后文放弃规则铺垫。正确答案。","[C] preserved（保留）：与变化趋势相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] defended（捍卫）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"objecting"},{"key":"B","text":"surrendering"},{"key":"C","text":"responding"},{"key":"D","text":"retreating"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (responding)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·介词搭配","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第1句","【解析】","[A] objecting（反对）：object to 语法正确，但公司是在回应而非反对用户行为。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] surrendering（投降）：surrender to 可通，但语气过强。程度差异干扰。","[C] responding（回应）：responding to changing user behaviour 是商业分析常用表达。正确答案。","[D] retreating（撤退）：retreat to 后多接地点或状态，语义不符。搭配干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"transactions"},{"key":"B","text":"promotions"},{"key":"C","text":"distractions"},{"key":"D","text":"connections"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (connections)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·上下文语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第1句","【解析】","[A] transactions（交易）：商业词，但约会应用目标是关系连接。语义场干扰。","[B] promotions（推广）：公司营销不是此处用户行为目标。语义场干扰。","[C] distractions（消遣）：方向偏离。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] connections（联系、情感连接）：meaningful connections 指更有意义的匹配与交流。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"reading"},{"key":"B","text":"copying"},{"key":"C","text":"banning"},{"key":"D","text":"pricing"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (reading)","analysis":["【题型】动名词辨析·熟词僻义","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第2句","【解析】","[A] reading（解读）：another way of reading the changes 中 read 是“解读”而非“阅读”。正确答案。","[B] copying（复制）：语义不通。语义场干扰。","[C] banning（禁止）：公司不是禁止变化。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] pricing（定价）：与产品策略解读无关。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"upgrading"},{"key":"B","text":"dismantling"},{"key":"C","text":"celebrating"},{"key":"D","text":"financing"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (dismantling)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·语义方向","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 5, 第1句","【解析】","[A] upgrading（升级）：与放弃原有特征的方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] dismantling（拆除、逐步取消）：dismantling those features 呼应前文 abandoned and softened。正确答案。","[C] celebrating（庆祝）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] financing（资助）：与取消功能无关。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"praised"},{"key":"B","text":"restored"},{"key":"C","text":"reworked"},{"key":"D","text":"banned"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (reworked)","analysis":["【题型】非谓语动词·被动进行","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 5, 第3句","【解析】","[A] praised（被赞扬）：与 quietly 和行业重构的语境不符。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] restored（被恢复）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] reworked（被改作、被重塑）：is being quietly reworked 指滑动匹配模式正在被悄悄改造。正确答案。","[D] banned（被禁止）：行业是调整而非禁止该模式。程度差异干扰。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语完型填空大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]}],"qa":[],"originals":[{"kind":"reading","label":"精读","file":"8.25 精读.pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":929743,"date":"2026-08-25","range":"","title":"Appy talk: what next for dating as swipe","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\8.25 精读.pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】8.25 检验题__阅读理解.docx","ext":".docx","bytes":55733,"date":"2026-08-25","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】8.25 检验题__阅读理解.docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】8.25检验题__完型填空.docx","ext":".docx","bytes":58202,"date":"2026-08-25","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】8.25检验题__完型填空.docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"layout","label":"杂志排版","file":"8.25杂志排版.pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":903155,"date":"2026-08-25","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\8.25杂志排版.pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"}]};
